      "id": "fixed-trailing-then-flow",
      "note": "A page fixed to the trailing side leaves the leading half free, but a flowing page MUST NOT take it: p2 follows p1 in the spine and the leading side is read first, so filling it would invert the reading order (section 10.4, spine-order invariant). The half-spread is emitted and p2 opens the next one.",
